  "id": "Compound::DB00443 - Disease::DOID:8893",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking Betamethasone to Psoriasis through a chain of biological interactions. Betamethasone is implicated in causing Scleral Thinning and Steroid Withdrawal Syndrome, both of which are associated with Hydrocortisone, which in turn is used to treat Psoriasis. This indicates a possible indirect pathway where Hydrocortisone, a corticosteroid, may exert a therapeutic effect on Psoriasis, possibly through anti-inflammatory or immunosuppressive mechanisms. The shared lowest common ancestor, Hydrocortisone, suggests a common biological pathway or functional role in the observed relationships. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Betamethasone and Psoriasis, though the exact mode of action remains unclear. The observed relationships are consistent with a broader class of corticosteroids, but the specific mechanisms by which Hydrocortisone treats Psoriasis require further investigation.",
